#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Fourth Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc03f48c-7f95-546a-9aa9-93b29e839962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242901} {:answer/id #uuid "aadd22e3-4946-555f-a5ef-8ad4b06bbe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242902} {:answer/id #uuid "865ff208-9bda-5e6f-9df1-d71ab2eeddcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242903} {:answer/id #uuid "4739b028-a4ff-57bf-a42b-cc2a72cf51d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242904} {:answer/id #uuid "10a8e9ec-047e-5ba2-957a-708df09f56e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10a8e9ec-047e-5ba2-957a-708df09f56e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242905} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b814a03-5aab-561f-ae2e-5dcc1016564f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "443ea97b-0750-5e83-b945-577ff014453b" :question/math-academy-id "q-170494" :question/problem "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=9-6\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/1bc5f38d44d9df32a7493f8d210bbc17d716d8a63316e3d730a1c4258d56fe46.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{6}{9})=arctan⁡(\\frac{2}{3})≈0.588\\,00.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.588\\,00≈5.70\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833ac63c-235b-5059-ab7c-56eb1e44d79e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Second Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "700aa052-5bda-5318-a176-5ea7dfe6f9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "700aa052-5bda-5318-a176-5ea7dfe6f9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242908} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1fca77-3e7f-53e3-960f-0060bd3b8855" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a50732f-9ccb-5a9f-8b9e-e2e1266f6493" :question/math-academy-id "q-319499" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-11+8\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/d3b5558c0268843618c52c588ffcf1c8012189041b17d52fadd6fe74c3526700.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{11} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{8}{11}) \\\\  & =0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -0.628\\text{ }796\\text{ }…≈2.51,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "833ac63c-235b-5059-ab7c-56eb1e44d79e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Second Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd881fba-5af0-5c8a-8787-c82bfdcf5fc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242911} {:answer/id #uuid "c2002a52-1e83-5344-b1bc-0baa7e781dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2002a52-1e83-5344-b1bc-0baa7e781dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242912} :answer-field/id #uuid "05787393-74e8-587e-8a1e-ad23ec25a881" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d6c23e8-dfa9-5cf0-bb09-7d2dc3e11620" :question/math-academy-id "q-319507" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=-5+5\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/f466a110eda3b07b50d988de6e46a541ad85d7ff64f43a6f056ea216752fa2d9.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{5} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Fourth Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f0d7a6-d8c3-5bf9-b154-1f1964a2d46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9f0d7a6-d8c3-5bf9-b154-1f1964a2d46a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242915} :answer-field/id #uuid "edf05e22-5e7d-56a1-a953-158c90e18a53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "019c203e-8df8-505f-8a2f-32d848d7aea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-319562" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=8-11\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/16408e6add22c687e3d2cf865908011602bfa87878fcbc3387c4ad3d22180e47.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{11}{8})=0.942\\,000…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.942\\,000≈5.34,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186242916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a560db4d-e9d3-5d89-b2cd-c886f32db9df" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Third Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bc63a2-6f6e-5b02-b4a6-f42c78450921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242918} {:answer/id #uuid "456b0aae-db26-58b3-8856-bdfa86bf36b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242919} {:answer/id #uuid "236a0a53-3192-535d-9fd3-3290d33c57e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242920} {:answer/id #uuid "9a94018f-de9e-5a63-a25b-86b1cfa37581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242921} {:answer/id #uuid "a09f194f-6555-5d25-a6ae-f275a2f228b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "236a0a53-3192-535d-9fd3-3290d33c57e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.07" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242920} :answer-field/id #uuid "d20c0c58-a337-5759-8c30-d318f715c97d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7a59ae6-0f77-5eca-9ada-6bc7a3f7a2c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74716" :question/problem "Find, in radians to two decimal places, the argument of $z=-3-4\\text{i}.$ \n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930486/assets/7eff12ed4bca73dc27f834b0740b5b2235440250e11427f911c8fc29c99fa1d7.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\pi <arg⁡(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha  & =arctan⁡(\\frac{4}{3})≈0.927\\,30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)≈\\pi +0.927\\,30≈4.07\n$$\n\nto two decimal places."}]}
